{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** You're climbing a staircase with `n` steps. Each move climbs **1 or 2** steps. In how many distinct ways can you reach the top?"
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/5b5bd440-c3f1-4ccc-b822-0bf2215c0531.svg",
      "alt": "ways[i] counts the ways to stand on step i. Step 0 and step 1 have one way each. To land on step i, the last move came from step i minus 1 or from step i minus 2, so ways[i] = ways[i-1] + ways[i-2]: 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8. For n = 5 the answer is 8.",
      "width": 755,
      "height": 357,
